# Day 05 — backend-bootstrap/.gitignore
#
# This directory uses LOCAL state on purpose (the backend cannot create
# itself), which makes this the one .gitignore in the lab that is genuinely
# load-bearing. terraform.tfstate here describes the bucket every other
# directory writes its state to.

# Terraform state — IAC-003 checks that this is here and that no .tfstate
# file is committed. State is a secrets liability, not a build artefact.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info

# Provider cache. Hundreds of MB, machine-specific, regenerated by init.
# This is the orphaned-disk-space trap of the day: every directory you ever
# ran init in still has one.
.terraform/

# Plan files. A saved plan can contain sensitive values in the clear.
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Your real variable values.
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example

# NOT IGNORED, DELIBERATELY: .terraform.lock.hcl
#
# The dependency lock file records the exact provider versions and their
# checksums. Committing it is what makes `terraform init` reproducible for
# everyone else and in CI. Day 04's .gitignore had it listed; that was wrong,
# and IAC-012 is the check that would have caught it.
